title: Balanced complete bipartite baseline
tags: ['baseline', 'book']
abstract: Deterministic graph family on 4n-2 vertices with zero red book excess and large blue excess. It is intended as a transparent diagnostic baseline under range-coverage scoring.
content: |
    def _solution_for_n(n: int) -> str:
        if not isinstance(n, int):
            raise TypeError("n must be an integer")
        if n < 2:
            raise ValueError("n must be at least 2")

        total_vertices = 4 * n - 2
        cut = 2 * n - 1
        bits = []
        for j in range(1, total_vertices):
            for i in range(j):
                across_cut = (i < cut) != (j < cut)
                bits.append("1" if across_cut else "0")
        return "".join(bits)

    def solution_batch() -> dict[int, str]:
        return {n: _solution_for_n(n) for n in range(22, 51)}
